 "notes": "Hydrology/sedimentation report on Lakes Marion and Moultrie; no named stratigraphic units, structures or aquifers. Recorded lakebed cores 1-6 (appendix 1, pp. 52-53; cores 7-20 continue in packet-02). Appendix 1 chemistry/texture rows were not recorded as intervals: blank cells are dropped in the text layer so values cannot be assigned to columns reliably. Table 3 (pp. 19-20) site numbers 2-9 are lost in the text layer, so core locations were taken from appendix 1 headers instead. Skipped general (non-SC) references (Barko, Brune, Glenn, Guy, Kemp, Martin, Nriagu, Perlman, Porterfield, Simmons, Stevens, Tolonen, USGS data reports).\nContinues appendix 1 (results of lakebed sediment sampling) from packet-01: cores 7-20 recorded with label, location as printed and corer penetration. Core 9 longitude is garbled in the text layer (80°30'^k\"), so its location was left out. Appendix 1 chemistry/texture rows not recorded as intervals because dropped blank cells make column assignment unreliable. Appendix 2 (pp. 59-78, 210Pb activity graphs) is unreadable text from plotted figures; nothing recorded.",
